Last reviewed: 2026-02-09

Sources:
- DB DDL: `scripts/create_memory_tables.py`
- API models/schemas: `demo/full-stack-fastapi-template/backend/app/models.py`

## Relational Model (Tables + FKs)

```mermaid
erDiagram
  workflow_bucket {
    text workflow_key PK
    text bucket_name
    timestamptz created_at
    timestamptz updated_at
  }

  task {
    uuid id PK
    text title
    text workflow_key
    text intent_key
    text goal
    text acceptance_criteria
    jsonb systems_touched
    text risk_level
    text status
    timestamptz created_at
    timestamptz last_touched_at
  }

  run {
    uuid id PK
    uuid task_id FK
    jsonb targets
    timestamptz started_at
    timestamptz ended_at
    text status
    text summary
  }

  run_event {
    bigint id PK
    uuid run_id FK
    timestamptz ts
    text type
    text message
    jsonb data
    bigint supersedes_event_id FK
  }

  library_item {
    uuid id PK
    text workflow_key
    text kind
    text title
    text body_mdc
    jsonb tags
    jsonb source_refs
    timestamptz created_at
    timestamptz last_used_at
    text promotion_mode
    uuid superseded_by_id FK
  }

  run_library_link {
    uuid run_id FK
    uuid library_item_id FK
    text relation
    timestamptz created_at
  }

  %% Grouping
  workflow_bucket ||--o{ task : "labels workflow_key (not FK-enforced)"
  workflow_bucket ||--o{ library_item : "labels workflow_key (not FK-enforced)"

  %% Execution/audit
  task ||--o{ run : has
  run ||--o{ run_event : logs
  run_event ||--o| run_event : supersedes

  %% Memory links + versioning
  run ||--o{ run_library_link : links
  library_item ||--o{ run_library_link : linked
  library_item ||--o| library_item : superseded_by
```

Notes:
- `workflow_key` is a **soft grouping key** today. There is no DB-level FK from `task.workflow_key` / `library_item.workflow_key` to `workflow_bucket.workflow_key`.
- `task.intent_key` is the recommended **Task grouping key** for deciding whether to reuse a Task (append a Run) or create a new Task.
- `run_event` is append-only by convention; corrections are modeled via `supersedes_event_id`.
- `library_item` is never deleted by convention; updates are modeled by inserting a new row and setting `superseded_by_id` on the old one.

## API Schema Composition (Object Graph)

```mermaid
classDiagram
  class TasksPublic {
    data: TaskPublic[]
    count: int
  }
  class TaskPublic {
    id: uuid
    workflow_key: string
    title: string
    intent_key: string?
    goal: string?
    acceptance_criteria: string?
    systems_touched: object
    risk_level: string
    status: string
    created_at: datetime?
    last_touched_at: datetime?
  }

  class RunsPublic {
    data: RunPublic[]
    count: int
  }
  class RunPublic {
    id: uuid
    task_id: uuid
    targets: any[]
    started_at: datetime?
    ended_at: datetime?
    status: string
    summary: string?
  }

  class RunDetailPublic {
    run: RunPublic
    events: RunEventPublic[]
    memory_links: RunMemoryLinkPublic[]
  }
  class RunEventPublic {
    id: int
    run_id: uuid
    ts: datetime?
    type: string
    message: string?
    data: object
    supersedes_event_id: int?
  }

class RunMemoryLinkPublic {
    relation: string
    created_at: datetime?
    library_item: LibraryItemPublic
  }
  class LibraryItemPublic {
    id: uuid
    workflow_key: string
    kind: string
    title: string
    body_mdc: string
    tags: object
    source_refs: any[]
    promotion_mode: string
    created_at: datetime?
    last_used_at: datetime?
    superseded_by_id: uuid?
  }

  TasksPublic --> TaskPublic
  RunsPublic --> RunPublic
  RunDetailPublic --> RunPublic
  RunDetailPublic --> RunEventPublic
  RunDetailPublic --> RunMemoryLinkPublic
  RunMemoryLinkPublic --> LibraryItemPublic
```

Enum notes (current API constraints):
- `library_item.kind`: `recipe|pitfall|decision|checklist`
- `library_item.promotion_mode`: `auto|user`
- `run_library_link.relation`: `used|created|promoted|superseded`
